spans.s:
khalaka,
(1) m. or nt. (= Skt. khala), threshing-floor or granary: Kv 〔28.18〕 (prose) mahā-khalake mahāntaṃ rāśiṃ kuryāt;
(2) m. (= Skt. khala; AMg. khalaya, app. in this sense, Ratnach.), rogue, or adj. roguish, evil, bad: perhaps read khalakā(ḥ) for text khaṇḍakā(ḥ) Mmk 〔73.13〕; see s.v. khaṇḍaka.
